    slug: "business-operations",
    title: "Business Operations: finances, compliance and documents",
    summary: "Keep your organization’s business profile, transactions, activities, compliance requirements and documents, and see them on a dashboard.",
    applicationKey: "platform",
    contentType: "how-to",
    category: "Business Operations",
    audience: ["admin"],
    tags: ["business operations", "finances", "compliance", "documents", "dashboards"],
    content: "# Who can use it\n\nBusiness Operations is for managers, administrators and owners, while the app is active for your organization. Members and staff can't open it. Your records are private to your organization; Zebron's platform administrators can open them to help you.\n\n# Getting started\n\n1. On the partner dashboard, open **Business Operations**.\n2. Click **Business profile** and enter the legal name, entity type and address. Everything else (transactions, activities, compliance, documents) belongs to a business, so the profile comes first.\n3. Add transactions, activities and compliance requirements, and upload documents (up to 25 MB each).\n\nThe address is kept on your business record, visible only to your organization's managers.\n\n# Compliance status\n\nEach night Zebron updates the status of requirements that have **automatic monitoring** switched on, from their due dates: upcoming, action required, overdue or expired. Others keep the status you set.\n\n# On a dashboard\n\nManagers can create a **Business overview** dashboard (Dashboards → New dashboard): revenue, expenses and net for this month, revenue and expenses by month (last 6 months), compliance needing attention and compliance by status. You can also add these figures to any dashboard as key figures or bar charts.\n\n- Figures count **completed** transactions only, in US dollars, across all your businesses.\n- They are updated every night; **⋮ → Refresh business figures** updates them now (at most every 10 minutes).\n- A negative net means more was spent than earned this month.",
