    content: "# The header menu\n\nOpen the menu (☰) at the top right of any page.\n\n- **Your name** is the first item. It opens your profile. (It used to say \"Profile\", with your name and role shown above it.)\n- **Platform** lists the Zebron applications you can open. The Tax & Pay Calculator is not listed there. The Learning Lab has become **Courses**.\n\n# Page titles\n\nThe large title in the header tells you where you are: an application name, your organization's name, or for example **\"Your Organization Learning\"** in the Test Center. The browser tab shows the specific page, such as the quiz you have open.\n\n# The home page\n\n- The **Resources & Services**, **Training & Education** and **Jobs & Opportunities** cards open the resources directory, the training search and the job search.\n- **From the Zebron Blog** shows three public posts: pinned posts first (marked **Featured**), then the newest. Click one to read it, or **Visit the blog** for all posts. The section is hidden until the blog has posts.\n\n# All apps and Popular\n\nThe **All apps** page lists every public Zebron application. The **Popular** section at the top shows:\n\n1. **Your favorites**, if you have any. Click the **star** on any app card to add it; click again to remove it.\n2. Otherwise, the **three apps you open most**.\n3. For first-time visitors, a few suggested apps.\n\nThe **Courses** card is in **Work and learning**, and the **Zebron Blog** card is in **Connect and get support**.\n\n> Favorites and the open counts are remembered in this browser only. On another computer or browser, Popular starts again.",
